List the per-sample results of a run.

Usage
  azd ai eval run output list [run] [flags]

Flags
      --after string            : Resume after this id, which the previous page printed.
      --all                     : Retrieve every page. Overrides --limit.
      --eval string             : Name of the eval declared in the configuration, or its id.
      --failed-only             : Show only the items that failed. Shorthand for --status failed.
      --limit int               : Rows per page. Defaults to 10.
      --output-file string      : Write JSON results to this path. Writes every row unless --limit narrows it.
      --path string             : Directory holding azure.eval.yaml. Defaults to the path init used, then ./evals.
      --project-endpoint string : Foundry project endpoint.
      --run string              : Run to act on. Defaults to the last run recorded for --eval.
      --status string           : Show only items with these outcomes: passed, failed, errored, skipped (comma-separated).

Global Flags
  -C, --cwd string         : Sets the current working directory
      --debug              : Enables debug and diagnostics logging
  -e, --environment string : The name of the environment to use
  -h, --help               : help for list
      --no-prompt          : Runs without prompts. Uses existing values; fails if any required value or decision cannot be resolved automatically.
  -o, --output string      : The output format (default "default")

Examples
  Inspect failed samples from the latest run
    azd ai eval run output list --eval quality --failed-only
